t passed on the  baton to a mars morales or a  spider-woman or something more diverse  then i would have done something wrong  in the sense of the sort of duties i  have to the character  not that like if i'm playing spider-man  in my 30s i'm like some washed up has  been that's not what i was saying only  making billion dollar movies every year  now yeah exactly  um so for me i  um  i i could see myself playing this  character into my 30s uh  i'm i'm very confident in in the films  and the project's capabilities to  succeed  and i think we have a really special  bit of material on our hands  so first things first tom holland  clarifies what he meant when he said  this quote a long time ago which is  great he doesn't mean that if he's 30  and still playing the same character  he's doing something wrong at least not  as an actor but as somebody who actually  cares about the character and about the  franchise what he meant was that if he's  still playing that character and other  people like miles morales and  spider-woman haven't come in then he's  doing a disservice to himself because he  is a fan but us as well as the other  fans but notice the last thing that he  said he said i can see myself playing  this character into my 30s and i'm very  confident in the films and project's  ability to succeed and then he said he  thinks they have a really special bit of  material on their hands this is great  news because he's talking about the  future of spider-man they just went  through an extremely special bit of  material the three spider-man on screen  live action for the very first time and  now he's saying they still have special  material left while at the same time  talking about how he thinks that  eventually the baton should be passed  down to a miles morales or a spider  woman now coincidentally olivia wilde is  set to direct a marvel spider-man film  it is currently untitled however many  people believe and rumor has it that it  is going to be a spider-woman film  following jessica drew and of course as  i've mentioned several times and as most  fans know miles morale morales  technically does exist inside of the mcu  because in spider-man homecoming we met  his uncle aaron davis aka the prowler  played by the childish gambino donald  glover who specifically mentions that he  has a nephew who of course is miles also  not to mention they dropped the miles  morales easter egg and spider-man no way  home where jamie foxx's electro says i  thought you were going to be black  there's got to be a black spider-man out  there somewhere so perhaps this is the  way that marvel studios plans to move  perhaps tom holland spider-man is going  to be sticking around for another one  two or three films hopefully another  trilogy but it looks like he is  eventually going to be passing that  baton off as he says to a different  spider-man or spider-woman which i'm  really excited to see now many of you  really loved spider-man knowing home and  in a different interview with the  hollywood reporter tom holland opened up  about two things that i really want to  talk about one he talked about how the  other two spider-men and the other two  actors really helped him and he talked  about a particular scene where he thanks  them in the film and then he talks about  andrew garfield's redemption arc in  spider-man no way home which i'll  actually talk about first because i  really love this because i really loved  andrew garfield spider-man in no way  home and i loved the fact that he  finally got his time and he finally did  get that redemption in the interview he  was asked one of the most heartwarming  aspects of no way home is the fact that  andrew is finally getting his due as  peter has the response to andrew's  performance been a source of pride for  you in which tom holland replied without  question i could not be happier for him  something i can look back on now with a  little bit of clarity and regret is that  i never called him when i took over as  spider-man had someone said to me after  my second movie that i was done and this  other kid was taking over i would have  been heartbroken so looking back i wish  i had the chance to make amends with him  but this film was our opportunity it was  not only an opportunity for him to make  peace with the character and the studio  but it was also an opportunity for me  and him to have this moment where we  realized we could share this thing the  look on his face when he saves zendaya  mj is totally genuine and i'm really  proud of him i'm really chuffed that he  got this opportunity to win back the  world and for people to be reminded that  his spider-man movies are fantastic and  brilliant in their own right now this i  absolutely  love because again i loved andrew  garfield in this movie and for tom to  say that andrew's face and his  expression when he caught mj was genuine  means that he was legitimately crying  and choked up over the fact that he  actually did get to save mj he couldn't  save gwen but he could save mj and i  think in a way he was kind of saving a  part of himself as well like in the  scene where toby is telling him that  he's amazing that's pretty meta it has  two different meanings not only is he  talking to spider-man as spider-man  making the little pun that he's amazing  hence the amazing spider-man but he's  also just toby mcguire talking to andrew  garfield saying hey dude your spider-man  was amazing your peter parker was  amazing you're amazing don't tell  yourself that your movies were bad you  are an amazing actor you were an amazing  spider-man and that's coming from the  original spider-man so i'm sure that  meant a lot to andrew garfield now the  second thing i want to talk about from  this interview is really really cool  it's where peter 1 is thanking peter 2  and peter 3. tom holland is asked in the  interview i love the moment where peter  says thank you thank you  thank you to peter 2 tobey maguire and  peter 3 andrew garfield he's obviously  saying thank you to those characters for  their help and their wisdom but i also  read it as you tom saying thank you to  toby and andrew for setting an example  and paving the way for your era as  spider-man was that in the back of your  mind at all while you filmed that  goodbye and this is what tom holland  said yeah that moment was actually  inspired by something that actually  happened we were on set shooting the  rooftop scene where i met the boys for  the first time and before one of the  takes it must have been my close-up or  something it was one that really really  required me to bring the emotion to the  shot so i went up to the two boys on the  level that they were standing and i said  to them thank you  thank you thank you for doing this thank  you for being here thank you for  elevating spider-man in the ways that  you have thank you for being so gracious  and allowing me to share this with you  thank you for taking a leap of faith and  coming back toby hadn't acted in nearly  10 years so we all embraced each other  and we were all crying because it meant  so much to us and john watts amy pascal  and the writer saw this moment between  the three of us and were like brilliant  well now we know how they're going to  say goodbye to each other so essentially  we just reshot that very real moment  between the three of us and i can't tell  you how much i absolutely love this and  i would just so  love to see some behind the scenes shots  of the three spider-men just hanging out  together and possibly crying together  like we just heard about that's kind of  all i want right now but let me know  what you think about what tom holland  said about the future of spider-man and  this touching moment between the three  spider-man actors don't forget to like  the video if you enjoyed it don't forget  to subscribe so you can stay up to date  on all other mcu news and for live  updates you can follow me on instagram  and twitter as always thank you all so  much for watching woof

